<h2 style="font-size: 28px; color: #1565c0; margin-top: 30px;">Examination Overview - NISM Series XIX-A: Alternative Investment Funds (Category I and II) Distributors Certification Mock Test</h2>
<br />

<p style="color: #000;">
The examination is designed to establish a minimum knowledge benchmark for professionals and aspiring candidates seeking to understand Alternative Investment Funds (AIFs) in India, specifically Category I and Category II funds, which play a crucial role in channelizing capital into sectors such as startups, infrastructure, and private equity.<br>

<br>This certification aims to enhance the understanding of the AIF ecosystem by covering key aspects such as fund structures, investment strategies, risk-return dynamics, governance frameworks, due diligence processes, valuation methodologies, taxation, and regulatory guidelines prescribed by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI). It ensures that candidates develop the ability to evaluate investment opportunities, assess risks, and understand the lifecycle of AIF investments from fundraising to exit.<br>

<br>By strengthening conceptual clarity around legal documentation, negotiation, fund monitoring, reporting standards, and investor servicing practices, the examination promotes informed decision-making and responsible participation in the alternative investments space. It also supports higher standards of transparency, compliance, and investor protection within the Indian financial ecosystem.
</p>
<h2 style="font-size: 22px; color: #1565c0; margin-top: 30px;">Examination Objectives</h2>
<br />
<p style="color: #000;">
  On successful completion of the examination, the candidate should be able to:
</p>

<div>

  <p style="color: #000;">
    <img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />
    Know the basics of alternative asset classes and the Alternative Investment Funds (Category I and II) markets in India.
  </p>

  <p style="color: #000;">
    <img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />
    Understand the general concepts prevalent in the Alternative Investment Funds (AIF) industry.
  </p>

  <p style="color: #000;">
    <img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />
    Structure, risk-return relationship, investment process, governance aspects, monitoring and exit strategies of AIFs.
  </p>

  <p style="color: #000;">
    <img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />
    Importance of fund due diligence, legal documentation, and negotiation skills along with assessment of risk and return.
  </p>

  <p style="color: #000;">
    <img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />
    Valuation processes and methodologies followed by AIFs for investee companies.
  </p>

  <p style="color: #000;">
    <img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />
    Various taxation aspects applicable to the fund and its investors.
  </p>

  <p style="color: #000;">
    <img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />
    Role and conduct of distributors in servicing investors.
  </p>

  <p style="color: #000;">
    <img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />
    Back-end processes including documentation and reporting.
  </p>

  <p style="color: #000;">
    <img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />
    Know the regulatory environment in which Alternative Investment Funds (Category I and II) operate in India.
  </p>

</div>



